# AWS CloudWatch Agent Setup on EC2

## Simple Step-by-Step Guide

Follow these steps in order. Complete one step first, then move to the next step.

---

## Step 1 — Create an IAM Role

Open:

**AWS Console → IAM → Roles → Create Role**

Select:

- **Trusted entity:** AWS service
- **Use case:** EC2

Attach this permission:

```text
CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy
```

Create the role and attach it to your EC2 instance.

---

## Step 2 — Connect to the EC2 Instance

Connect to your Ubuntu EC2 instance using SSH or EC2 Instance Connect.

---

## Step 3 — Update Ubuntu Packages

Run:

```bash
sudo apt update -y
```

---

## Step 4 — Download the CloudWatch Agent

For Ubuntu 64-bit, run:

```bash
wget https://amazoncloudwatch-agent.s3.amazonaws.com/ubuntu/amd64/latest/amazon-cloudwatch-agent.deb
```

---

## Step 5 — Install the CloudWatch Agent

Run:

```bash
sudo dpkg -i -E ./amazon-cloudwatch-agent.deb
```

---

## Step 6 — Open the Configuration Wizard

Run:

```bash
sudo /opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/bin/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-config-wizard
```

For a basic EC2 practical, you can select:

```text
CollectD: No
StatsD: No
```

Complete the wizard. It will create a configuration file.

---

## Step 7 — Start the CloudWatch Agent

If your configuration file is:

```text
/opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/bin/config.json
```

Run:

```bash
sudo /opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/bin/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ctl \
-a fetch-config \
-m ec2 \
-s \
-c file:/opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/bin/config.json
```

---

## Step 8 — Check Agent Status

Run:

```bash
sudo /opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/bin/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ctl \
-a status \
-m ec2
```

The agent should show that it is running.

---

## Step 9 — Install the Stress Tool

Run:

```bash
sudo apt install stress -y
```

---

## Step 10 — Generate CPU Load

Run:

```bash
stress --cpu 1
```

Stop the stress test with:

```text
Ctrl + C
```

---

## Step 11 — Check Metrics in CloudWatch

Open:

**AWS Console → CloudWatch → Metrics → All metrics**

Select the metrics for your EC2 instance and check whether data is appearing.

---

## Important

- Do not upload AWS Access Keys, Secret Keys or passwords to GitHub.
- Attach the required IAM role to EC2 so the CloudWatch Agent can send metrics.
- Stop stress testing after completing the monitoring test.
